\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\\,✓\n$$\n\n \nThus, equation I is exact.\n\n- The second equation is\n\n$$\n({y}^{2}+x)\\,\\text{d}x+(xy+1)\\,\\text{d}y=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the functions $P$ and $Q$ are\n\n$$\nP(x,y)={y}^{2}+x,\\,Q(x,y)=xy+1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}+x) \\\\  & =2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy+1) \\\\  & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\ne \\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nThus, equation II is not exact.\n\n- The third equation is\n\n$$\n(5y-3x)\\,\\text{d}y-(y-2x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the functions $P$ and $Q$ are\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=-(y-2x)=2x-y,\\,Q(x,y)=5y-3x.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x-y) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(5y-3x) \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSo,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\ne \\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nThus, equation III is not exact.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." 13194139535258 true] [17592186340262 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340263 13194139535258 true] [17592186340262 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340264 13194139535258 true] [17592186340262 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340265 13194139535258 true] [17592186340262 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340266 13194139535258 true] [17592186340262 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340267 13194139535258 true] [17592186340262 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535258 true] [17592186340262 1041 "selection" 13194139535258 true] [17592186340262 1104 #edb/ref 17592186340264 13194139535258 true] [17592186340262 1110 #uuid "9d0b19d8-cbca-5872-8304-630cd1975f10" 13194139535258 true] [17592186340263 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535258 true] [17592186340263 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535258 true] [17592186340263 1111 #uuid "ce1c208e-1795-599f-a7c0-ba461be4a7f8" 13194139535258 true] [17592186340264 10