, we rearrange the terms:\n\n$$\n(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+5)\\,\\text{d}x+(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-4y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nNow, we should check for exactness. A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nFor our differential equation, we have\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+5,\\,Q(x,y)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-4y.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+5) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-4y) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\\,✓\n$$\n\nThus, our equation is exact.\n\nSince the equation is exact, our solution $u(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂u}{∂x}=P(x,y),\\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y}=Q(x,y)\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\int (y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+5)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)+5x+f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $y.$  Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\int (x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-4y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-2{y}^{2}+g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we see that we must have\n\n$$\ng(x)=5x,\\,f(y)=-2{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y)=c$ is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-2{y}^{2}+5x=c.\n$$\n\nThe particular solution specified by the initial condition must have $y=-2$ when $x=0.$ These values determine the value of the constant $c.$ Substituting this into the equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-2{y}^{2}+5x & =c \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(0\\cdot (-2))-2(-2)^{2}+5\\cdot 0 & =c \\\\ c & =0-8 \\\\ c & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-2{y}^{2}+5x=-8.\n$$" 13194139535258 true] [17592186340308 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340309 13194139535258 true] [17592186340308 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340310 13194139535258 true] [17592186340308 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340311 13194139535258 true] [17592186340308 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340312 13194139535258 true] [17592186340308 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340313 13194139535258 true] [17592186340308 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535258 true] [17592186340308 1041 "selection" 13194139535258 true] [17592186340308 1104 #edb/ref 17592186340309 13194139535258 true] [17592186340308 1110 #uuid "cf00bbf6-0040-55ba-ad7c-dcdb06503f06" 13194139535258 true] [17592186340309 1034 "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-2{y}^{2}+5x=-8" 13194139535258 true] [17592186340309 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535258 true] [17592186340309 1111 #uuid "c058c67f-ecc8-5cec-94de-69359cf44a72" 13194139535258 true] [17592186340310 1034 "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)+2{y}^{2}+5x=8" 13194139535258 true] [17592186340310 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535258 true] [17592186340310 1111 #uuid "018801e3-a35a-5324-a90b-6a16702969ce" 13194139535258 true] [17592186340311 1034 "{y}^{2}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-5x=4" 13194139535258 true] [17592186340311 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535258 true] [17592186340311 1111 #uuid "4e4036dd-e83a-5933-9347-609b6797dfd4" 13194139535258 true] [17592186340312 1034 "({y}^{2}-5x)\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)=0" 13194139535258 true] [17592186340312 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535258 true] [17592186340312 1111 #uuid "56bd45c9-197a-5393-b0f1-568ee4ba8e3f" 13194139535258 true] [17592186340313 1034 "{y}^{2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-5x=3" 13194139535258 true] [175921